      - win_spawn.h: posix_spawn for Windows on CreateProcessW (the user,
        2026-11-05; EXPERIMENTAL, not yet built into the module: that needs a
        Windows Perl).  Spawner.xs includes it under _WIN32 and #defines the
        posix_spawn names to it (#define posix_spawn win_posix_spawn and so
        on), so __posix_spawn is one source; no SIGCHLD helpers there.  The
        child's fds 0-2 through STARTUPINFO, fds 3 and up through the C
        runtime's lpReserved2 table, exactly the handles it should have
        through PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_HANDLE_LIST (inheritable copies made for
        the call); the file actions in order (open by the parent, relative to
        the child's directory; chdir, fchdir, closefrom); argv quoted as the C
        runtime parses it back; posix_spawnp through PATH and PATHEXT;
        pgroup 0 as CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP; ENOTSUP for a non-empty sigmask,
