      - Proc::Spawner::spawn does what the spawn primitive lacks around the
        call (the user, 2026-11-05: as a Windows port will have to):
        $Proc::Spawner::MISSING, a bitmap of the settings the primitive lacks
        (this libc's gaps, plus PROC_SPAWNER_MISSING for tests).  chdir,
        fchdir, the fd actions (dup2, close, open, closefrom), sigmask,
        sigdefault, pgroup => PGID, resetids, search and pidfd are done in
        this process around the call and undone; setsid, tcsetpgrp,
        pgroup => 0, sched and cgroup are unsupported (drop or fail).  New
