        skipped where unsupported.
      - Z0 (the user, 2026-11-05): printf's 0 flag with %s, %c or %b (printf
        '%0.s-' 1 2 3, a common way to repeat a character; %05s) is dropped
        before the program printf runs, so it pads with blanks, as glibc's
        printf(3) and both shells; coreutils refuses it ("invalid conversion
        specification").  The flag is undefined there in C and POSIX
        (large-subset-state.md, section 1).
      - large-subset-builtins.pl: a command name starting with - or + is
        quoted, and plain names after export, readonly, unset, local stay bare
